---
/**
 * 영어 안전한 이유 페이지 (/en/safety/). 한국어판(src/pages/safety.astro)과 같은 내용을 영어로 쓴다.
 */
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../site.config';

const localOnlyTest = `${siteConfig.sourceUrl}/blob/main/tests/e2e/local-only.ts`;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Why your files are safe"
  description={`How ${siteConfig.name} works without uploading your files, and how to check it yourself in your browser.`}
>
  <p>
    None of the tools on {siteConfig.name} upload your files, because there is no server that
    processes them at all. This page explains how that works, and how you can check it yourself
    instead of taking our word for it.
  </p>

  <h2>How is this different from typical online tools?</h2>
  <p>
    Many online PDF and image tools take your file, process it on the company's server, and send the
    result back. Here, your own browser does the work.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th></th>
        <th>Typical online tools</th>
        <th>{siteConfig.name}</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th>Where your file goes</th>
        <td>Uploaded to the company's server</td>
        <td>Never leaves your device</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Where it is processed</th>
        <td>The company's server</td>
        <td>Your browser</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>After processing</th>
        <td>How long it stays depends on the company's policy</td>
        <td>There is no server for it to stay on</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Waiting time</th>
        <td>Upload and download time + processing</td>
        <td>Processing only (depends on your device)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Sign-up or install</th>
        <td>Varies by tool</td>
        <td>Not needed</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>How does it work without a server?</h2>
  <p>
    Modern browsers can run programs on their own. When you open a tool page, the program that reads
    and edits PDFs is downloaded from this site into your browser, and it processes your file in
    your device's memory. The result is also created inside the browser and saved straight to your
    downloads.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Tool programs, Korean fonts, and text recognition (OCR) data all come from this site. Nothing
      is loaded from other companies' servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      Large downloads such as fonts and OCR data show their size before downloading, and are used
      only after checking that their content has not been changed.
    </li>
    <li>
      Heavy work runs in a separate background thread (Web Worker), so the page does not freeze
      while it is processing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Is it safe even with ads?</h2>
  <p>
    Ads pay for running the site. Ad scripts can read text on the same page, so the tool area is
    kept apart from the page.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The tool area, where you choose, preview, process, and download files, runs in an isolated
      space locked by the browser (a sandboxed iframe). Ads and visitor statistics scripts cannot
      look inside.
    </li>
    <li>
      Inside that space, browser security rules (CSP) block connections to any address other than
      this site's own files. Even the tool itself cannot send your file anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>File names and contents are never put in addresses, page titles, or visitor statistics.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to check it yourself</h2>
  <p>
    You don't have to take our word for it. Your computer's browser developer tools show every
    address the page talks to.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open a tool page (for example, Merge PDF) in Chrome or Edge. Press F12 on Windows or Cmd +
      Option + I on Mac to open the developer tools.
    </li>
    <li>Choose the Network tab at the top. Every request from now on is listed there.</li>
    <li>
      Clear the list with the clear button (a circle with a slash), then add a file to the tool,
      process it, and download the result.
    </li>
    <li>
      Click each new request to see its address. The tool's requests only download tool programs
      from
      {siteConfig.domain}, and none of them send out anything the size of your file.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    You may also see ad or statistics addresses. Those are called by the page outside the tool and
    cannot reach your files. In Safari, turn on the developer features in Settings → Advanced to get
    the same view.
  </p>

  <h2>The code is public</h2>
  <p>
    The source code of this site is public on <a href={siteConfig.sourceUrl}>GitHub</a>, so anyone
    can read it. Every time the site changes, automated tests run the tools in a real browser, and a
    <a href={localOnlyTest}>request check</a> confirms that no request carried a file name or file
    content and that the tool area connected nowhere but this site. Changes that fail this check do
    not reach the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot promise</h2>
  <p>To be honest, there are cases this site cannot prevent.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Browser extensions can read any page, depending on their permissions. When handling sensitive
      documents, keep only extensions you trust turned on.
    </li>
    <li>
      Processing uses your device's memory and power. Very large files may take a long time, or may
      not work on older phones.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tool programs are downloaded from this site as you use them, so you need an internet
      connection while processing. What is downloaded is the program, not your file.
    </li>
    <li>
      Downloaded results are saved on your device, so keeping them safe from then on depends on your
      device's security.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>
